# 設定画面の説明（1.8.9 で、それまで @Config.Comment だけだった項目にも足した）
weakspot.server.mining.boostmultiplier=Mining speed multiplier
weakspot.server.mining.boostmultiplier.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMining speed multiplier after a hit (the extra part is also scaled by the combo factor)\nFile: server.mining.boostMultiplier
weakspot.server.mining.boostdurationticks=Boost duration (ticks)
weakspot.server.mining.boostdurationticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHow long the multiplier lasts (ticks). One hit digs (multiplier - 1) x this many ticks' worth\nFile: server.mining.boostDurationTicks
weakspot.server.mining.weakspotradiusratio=Spot radius ratio
weakspot.server.mining.weakspotradiusratio.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nWeak spot radius (ratio to the shorter side of the face)\nFile: server.mining.weakSpotRadiusRatio
weakspot.server.mining.edgemargin=Edge margin
weakspot.server.mining.edgemargin.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum gap between the weak spot and the edge of the face (blocks)\nLarger values keep spots near the center; too large shortens how far they move\nFile: server.mining.edgeMargin
weakspot.server.mining.minmovedistance=Min move distance
weakspot.server.mining.minmovedistance.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum distance a weak spot moves after a hit (blocks)\nFile: server.mining.minMoveDistance
weakspot.server.mining.weakspotminradius=Min spot radius
weakspot.server.mining.weakspotminradius.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum weak spot radius (blocks), so small faces like buttons stay hittable\nThe maximum (weakSpotMaxRadiusRatio) wins if they conflict\nFile: server.mining.weakSpotMinRadius
weakspot.server.mining.weakspotmaxradiusratio=Max spot radius ratio
weakspot.server.mining.weakspotmaxradiusratio.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMaximum weak spot radius (ratio to the shorter side), so spots stay inside small faces\nFile: server.mining.weakSpotMaxRadiusRatio
weakspot.server.mining.minfacesize=Min face size
weakspot.server.mining.minfacesize.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nShortest side a face needs for a weak spot (blocks). Smaller faces (carpet sides, etc.) get none\n0 shows spots on any face\nFile: server.mining.minFaceSize
weakspot.server.mining.lingerticks=Linger time (ticks)
weakspot.server.mining.lingerticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHow long a weak spot stays after you stop holding (ticks)\nFile: server.mining.lingerTicks
weakspot.server.mining.minhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.mining.minhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted mining hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.mining.minHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.repair.hitsperrepair=Hits per repair
weakspot.server.repair.hitsperrepair.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nWhen you break a block, every this many mining hits on it repairs the held tool\nHits on blocks you did not break do not count. The remainder carries over. 0 disables repair\nFile: server.repair.hitsPerRepair
weakspot.server.repair.repairperstep=Repair per step
weakspot.server.repair.repairperstep.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nDurability repaired per hitsPerRepair\nFile: server.repair.repairPerStep
weakspot.server.repair.maxrepairperbreak=Max repair per break
weakspot.server.repair.maxrepairperbreak.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMaximum durability repaired per broken block. Anything above is dropped\n0 disables repair (milestone rewards still apply)\nFile: server.repair.maxRepairPerBreak
weakspot.server.milestones.milestones=Mining milestones
weakspot.server.milestones.milestones.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTotal mining hits that count as milestones. Each gives a celebration and rewards once\nmilestoneXp and milestoneRepair follow this order. Per-kind milestones use the same numbers\nFile: server.milestones.milestones
weakspot.server.milestones.milestonexp=Milestone XP
weakspot.server.milestones.milestonexp.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nExperience for each milestone (same order as milestones)\nMissing entries count as 0\nFile: server.milestones.milestoneXp
weakspot.server.milestones.milestonerepair=Milestone repair
weakspot.server.milestones.milestonerepair.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nDurability repaired on the held tool for each milestone (same order as milestones; mining only)\nMissing entries count as 0\nFile: server.milestones.milestoneRepair
weakspot.server.milestones.milestonerepeatinterval=Milestone repeat interval
weakspot.server.milestones.milestonerepeatinterval.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nAfter the largest milestone, a milestone every this many hits. 0 stops repeating\nThe reward is the last milestoneXp / milestoneRepair value\nFile: server.milestones.milestoneRepeatInterval
weakspot.server.milestones.kindmilestonesenabled=Per-kind milestones
weakspot.server.milestones.kindmilestonesenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nAlso give milestones for each kind other than mining, using the milestones numbers\nThe reward is experience only (milestoneXp)\nFile: server.milestones.kindMilestonesEnabled
weakspot.server.milestones.totalmilestonesenabled=Total milestones on
weakspot.server.milestones.totalmilestonesenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nAlso give milestones for the total hits of all kinds (numbers in totalMilestones)\nFile: server.milestones.totalMilestonesEnabled
weakspot.server.milestones.totalmilestones=Total milestones
weakspot.server.milestones.totalmilestones.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTotal hits of all kinds that count as total milestones\ntotalMilestoneXp follows this order\nFile: server.milestones.totalMilestones
weakspot.server.milestones.totalmilestonexp=Total milestone XP
weakspot.server.milestones.totalmilestonexp.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nExperience for each total milestone (same order as totalMilestones)\nMissing entries count as 0\nFile: server.milestones.totalMilestoneXp
weakspot.server.milestones.totalmilestonerepeatinterval=Total repeat interval
weakspot.server.milestones.totalmilestonerepeatinterval.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nAfter the largest total milestone, one every this many hits. 0 stops repeating\nThe reward is the last totalMilestoneXp value\nFile: server.milestones.totalMilestoneRepeatInterval
weakspot.server.growth.growthticksperhit=Growth ticks per hit
weakspot.server.growth.growthticksperhit.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nExtra random ticks given to a crop or sapling per growth hit\nUnlike bone meal, growth conditions such as light and farmland moisture still apply\nFile: server.growth.growthTicksPerHit
weakspot.server.growth.growthwarnings=Growth warnings
weakspot.server.growth.growthwarnings.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTell the player in chat when growth hits do not make a plant grow\nToo dark (light below 9 for crops, stems and saplings): on the first hit; otherwise after growthStuckHits hits without change\nFile: server.growth.growthWarnings
weakspot.server.growth.growthstuckhits=Hits before warning
weakspot.server.growth.growthstuckhits.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHits without any change before warning that something else stops the plant from growing\nFile: server.growth.growthStuckHits
weakspot.server.growth.growthminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.growth.growthminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted growth hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.growth.growthMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.growth.growthminradius=Min spot radius
weakspot.server.growth.growthminradius.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum radius of growth weak spots (blocks), so small faces stay hittable\nFile: server.growth.growthMinRadius
weakspot.server.growth.growthexcludedblocks=Excluded blocks
weakspot.server.growth.growthexcludedblocks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nBlock IDs that never get growth weak spots (also applies to sugar cane, cactus and nether wart)\nBy default, blocks with IGrowable that are not crops (grass block, grass, ...) are excluded\nFile: server.growth.growthExcludedBlocks
weakspot.server.growth.mushroomgrowchance=Mushroom grow chance
weakspot.server.growth.mushroomgrowchance.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nChance (0-1) that one growth hit on a mushroom tries to grow a huge mushroom (same as one bone meal)\nVanilla conditions apply; if it fails, the mushroom stays\nFile: server.growth.mushroomGrowChance
weakspot.server.growth.growthextrablocks=Extra blocks
weakspot.server.growth.growthextrablocks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nExtra blocks that get growth weak spots; hits give them extra random ticks\nOne per line: "id" or "id[property=condition,...]". Conditions: 0-6 (range), dry_* (* matches anything), or an exact value\nExample: somemod:crop[age=0-6]. Without conditions it always shows (nether wart defaults to age=0-2, ic2:rubber_wood to state=dry_*;\nsugar cane and cactus height is checked in code). Do not add blocks that use random ticks for other things (leaves, grass, farmland, ice)\nBlocks in growthExcludedBlocks are excluded even if listed here\nFile: server.growth.growthExtraBlocks
weakspot.server.machine.machineboostmultiplier=Machine speed multiplier
weakspot.server.machine.machineboostmultiplier.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHow many times per tick update() runs on a hit machine (4.0 = 3 extra calls per tick)\nIf several players boost the same machine, the larger value is used, not the sum\nFile: server.machine.machineBoostMultiplier
weakspot.server.machine.machineboostmaxmultiplier=Max multiplier
weakspot.server.machine.machineboostmaxmultiplier.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMaximum machine multiplier. Also sent to clients (the "Machine Nx speed" label). Combos multiply machineBoostMultiplier\n(x1.25 at 25, x1.5 at 50, x2 at 100, x2.5 at 250, x3 at 500, x4 at 1000), capped by this value\nLower it if a machine mod misbehaves or the server is under load. It wins even when below machineBoostMultiplier\nFile: server.machine.machineBoostMaxMultiplier
weakspot.server.machine.machineboostparticles=Boost particles
weakspot.server.machine.machineboostparticles.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nShow colored particles around boosted machines (visible to nearby players,\nexcept those who turned machineParticlesVisible off). Server only (not sent to clients)\nFile: server.machine.machineBoostParticles
weakspot.server.machine.machineboostdurationticks=Boost duration (ticks)
weakspot.server.machine.machineboostdurationticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHow long a machine boost lasts (ticks). At machineMinHitIntervalTicks or more, hitting at the fastest pace never lets it drop\nFile: server.machine.machineBoostDurationTicks
weakspot.server.machine.machineminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.machine.machineminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted machine hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.machine.machineMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.machine.excludedblocks=Excluded blocks
weakspot.server.machine.excludedblocks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nBlock IDs that machines boosting ignores. Sneaking with an empty hand opens their GUI as usual\nAdd machines that break when boosted\nFile: server.machine.excludedBlocks
weakspot.server.animal.animalbabyenabled=Baby growth
weakspot.server.animal.animalbabyenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nAnimal weak spots speed up babies growing up\nFile: server.animal.animalBabyEnabled
weakspot.server.animal.animalbreedingenabled=Breeding cooldown
weakspot.server.animal.animalbreedingenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nAnimal weak spots shorten the breeding cooldown\nFile: server.animal.animalBreedingEnabled
weakspot.server.animal.sheepwoolenabled=Wool regrowth
weakspot.server.animal.sheepwoolenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nSheep weak spots regrow wool faster (no grass needed)\nFile: server.animal.sheepWoolEnabled
weakspot.server.animal.chickeneggenabled=Chicken eggs
weakspot.server.animal.chickeneggenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nChicken weak spots shorten the time to the next egg\nFile: server.animal.chickenEggEnabled
weakspot.server.animal.villagertraderesetenabled=Villager trade reset
weakspot.server.animal.villagertraderesetenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nVillager weak spots reset the limits of locked trades\nFile: server.animal.villagerTradeResetEnabled
weakspot.server.animal.animalbabyhits=Hits to grow up
weakspot.server.animal.animalbabyhits.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nAbout how many hits turn a baby into an adult (one hit = 24000 ticks / this)\n0 or less disables it\nFile: server.animal.animalBabyHits
weakspot.server.animal.animalbreedinghits=Hits to breed again
weakspot.server.animal.animalbreedinghits.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nAbout how many hits end the breeding cooldown (one hit = 6000 ticks / this)\n0 or less disables it\nFile: server.animal.animalBreedingHits
weakspot.server.animal.sheepwoolhits=Hits to regrow wool
weakspot.server.animal.sheepwoolhits.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHits for a sheared sheep to regrow its wool\n0 or less disables it\nFile: server.animal.sheepWoolHits
weakspot.server.animal.chickenegghits=Hits to next egg
weakspot.server.animal.chickenegghits.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nAbout how many hits until the next egg (one hit = 9000 ticks on average / this)\n0 or less disables it\nFile: server.animal.chickenEggHits
weakspot.server.animal.villagertraderesethits=Hits to reset trades
weakspot.server.animal.villagertraderesethits.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHits to reset the limits of a villager's locked trades\n0 or less disables it\nFile: server.animal.villagerTradeResetHits
weakspot.server.animal.animalminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.animal.animalminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted animal hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.animal.animalMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.animal.animalexcludedentities=Excluded entities
weakspot.server.animal.animalexcludedentities.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nEntity IDs that never get animal weak spots (e.g. minecraft:cow)\nRight clicking them works as usual\nFile: server.animal.animalExcludedEntities
weakspot.server.animal.animalsneakrequiredentities=Sneak-only entities
weakspot.server.animal.animalsneakrequiredentities.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nModded animal entity IDs that only show weak spots while sneaking with an empty hand\nAdd animals whose empty-hand right click does something else (ride, open an inventory, sit). Vanilla horses, tamed wolves, etc. are handled in code\nFile: server.animal.animalSneakRequiredEntities
weakspot.server.animal.villagerresetunlocksnewtier=Unlock new trade tier
weakspot.server.animal.villagerresetunlocksnewtier.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nResetting a villager's trade limits also unlocks a new trade tier (like vanilla restocking)\nOff: only unlocks locked trades. Server only (not sent to clients)\nFile: server.animal.villagerResetUnlocksNewTier
weakspot.server.fishing.fishingweakspotenabled=Fishing weak spots
weakspot.server.fishing.fishingweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the fishing weak spots on or off\nFile: server.fishing.fishingWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.fishing.fishinghits=Hits to zero wait
weakspot.server.fishing.fishinghits.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHits that cut the longest wait (600 ticks) to zero (one hit = 600 ticks / this)\n0 or less disables fishing weak spots\nFile: server.fishing.fishingHits
weakspot.server.fishing.fishingminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.fishing.fishingminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted fishing hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.fishing.fishingMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.bow.bowweakspotenabled=Bow weak spots
weakspot.server.bow.bowweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the bow weak spots on or off\nFile: server.bow.bowWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.bow.bowhitticks=Draw ticks per hit
weakspot.server.bow.bowhitticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTicks of bow draw added per hit (a vanilla bow is fully drawn after 20 ticks)\nNever goes past full draw. 0 disables bow weak spots\nFile: server.bow.bowHitTicks
weakspot.server.bow.bowminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.bow.bowminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted bow hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.bow.bowMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.sleep.sleepweakspotenabled=Sleeping weak spots
weakspot.server.sleep.sleepweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the sleeping weak spots on or off\nWhile sleeping at night, a marker shows on the sleep screen. Clicking it moves the world time forward (for everyone)\nFile: server.sleep.sleepWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.sleep.sleephitticks=Ticks per hit
weakspot.server.sleep.sleephitticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nWorld time added per sleeping hit (ticks). Never goes past the next morning\nServer only (not sent to clients)\nFile: server.sleep.sleepHitTicks
weakspot.server.sleep.sleepminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.sleep.sleepminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted sleeping hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.sleep.sleepMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.eat.eatweakspotenabled=Eating weak spots
weakspot.server.eat.eatweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the eating and drinking weak spots on or off\nWhile eating or drinking, a weak spot shows near the crosshair. Hits shorten the time to finish\nFile: server.eat.eatWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.eat.eathitticks=Ticks cut per hit
weakspot.server.eat.eathitticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTicks removed from eating or drinking per hit. Vanilla food takes 32 ticks, so 16 finishes in 2 hits\nFile: server.eat.eatHitTicks
weakspot.server.eat.eatminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.eat.eatminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted eating hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.eat.eatMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleweakspotenabled=Vehicle weak spots
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the vehicle weak spots on or off\nWhile riding a moving horse, pig, minecart or boat, a weak spot shows near the crosshair. Hits speed it up for a while\nFile: server.vehicle.vehicleWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleboostmultiplier=Speed multiplier
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleboostmultiplier.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nVehicle speed multiplier after a hit, scaled by the combo factor (x1.25 at 25 ... x4 at 1000)\nFile: server.vehicle.vehicleBoostMultiplier
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleboostmaxmultiplier=Max multiplier
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleboostmaxmultiplier.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMaximum vehicle speed multiplier. 0 means no limit (default; x6 at combo 1000)\nSet 3.0 or so if it gets too fast\nFile: server.vehicle.vehicleBoostMaxMultiplier
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleboostdurationticks=Boost duration (ticks)
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleboostdurationticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHow long a vehicle boost lasts (ticks). Each hit resets it\nFile: server.vehicle.vehicleBoostDurationTicks
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.vehicle.vehicleminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted vehicle hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.vehicle.vehicleMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderweakspotenabled=Ladder weak spots
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the ladder weak spots on or off\nWhile climbing a ladder or vines, a weak spot shows straight above or below the crosshair. Hits speed up climbing for a while\nFile: server.ladder.ladderWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderboostmultiplier=Speed multiplier
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderboostmultiplier.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nClimbing speed multiplier after a hit, scaled by the combo factor (x1.25 at 25 ... x4 at 1000)\nFile: server.ladder.ladderBoostMultiplier
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderboostmaxmultiplier=Max multiplier
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderboostmaxmultiplier.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMaximum climbing speed multiplier. 0 means no limit (default)\nSet 3.0 or so if it gets too fast\nFile: server.ladder.ladderBoostMaxMultiplier
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderboostdurationticks=Boost duration (ticks)
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderboostdurationticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHow long a climbing boost lasts (ticks). Each hit resets it\nFile: server.ladder.ladderBoostDurationTicks
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.ladder.ladderminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted ladder hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.ladder.ladderMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.elytra.elytraweakspotenabled=Elytra weak spots
weakspot.server.elytra.elytraweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the elytra weak spots on or off\nWhile flying with an elytra, a weak spot shows near the crosshair. Hits launch you where you look\nFile: server.elytra.elytraWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.elytra.elytraboostpower=Boost power
weakspot.server.elytra.elytraboostpower.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nSpeed added per elytra hit (blocks/tick), scaled by the combo factor\nNo speed limit\nFile: server.elytra.elytraBoostPower
weakspot.server.elytra.elytraminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.elytra.elytraminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted elytra hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.elytra.elytraMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.enchant.enchantweakspotenabled=Enchanting weak spots
weakspot.server.enchant.enchantweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the enchanting weak spots on or off\nWith an item on an enchanting table, a marker shows on the screen. Clicking it rerolls the three offers (costs nothing)\nFile: server.enchant.enchantWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.enchant.enchantminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.enchant.enchantminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted enchanting hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.enchant.enchantMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.harvest.harvestweakspotenabled=Harvest weak spots
weakspot.server.harvest.harvestweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the harvest weak spots on or off\nHolding right click with an empty hand on a ripe crop shows a weak spot. Hits harvest and replant it\nTurn it off if another mod (such as Quark) already harvests on right click\nFile: server.harvest.harvestWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.harvest.harvestminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.harvest.harvestminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted harvest hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.harvest.harvestMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.harvest.harvestcombobonus=Combo bonus drops
weakspot.server.harvest.harvestcombobonus.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMultiply harvest drops by the combo factor (x1.25 at 25 ... x4 at 1000; seeds are not multiplied)\nServer only (not sent to clients)\nFile: server.harvest.harvestComboBonus
weakspot.server.throw.throwweakspotenabled=Throwing weak spots
weakspot.server.throw.throwweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the throwing weak spots on or off\nWhile holding ender pearls, snowballs, eggs, potions or bottles o' enchanting, a weak spot shows near the crosshair\nEach hit charges up; the next throw flies faster and farther (kept until you switch items, used up when thrown)\nFile: server.throw.throwWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.throw.throwchargeperhit=Charge per hit
weakspot.server.throw.throwchargeperhit.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nCharge added per throwing hit (added to the throw speed multiplier), scaled by the combo factor\nNo charge limit\nFile: server.throw.throwChargePerHit
weakspot.server.throw.throwminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.throw.throwminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted throwing hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.throw.throwMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintweakspotenabled=Sprint weak spots
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the sprint weak spots on or off\nWhile sprinting on the ground, a weak spot shows straight above or below the crosshair. Hits make you run faster for a while\nFile: server.sprint.sprintWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintboostmultiplier=Speed multiplier
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintboostmultiplier.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nSprint speed multiplier after a hit, scaled by the combo factor (x1.25 at 25 ... x4 at 1000)\nFile: server.sprint.sprintBoostMultiplier
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintboostmaxmultiplier=Max multiplier
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintboostmaxmultiplier.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMaximum sprint speed multiplier. 0 means no limit (default)\nSet 3.0 or so if it gets too fast\nFile: server.sprint.sprintBoostMaxMultiplier
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintboostdurationticks=Boost duration (ticks)
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintboostdurationticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHow long a sprint boost lasts (ticks). Each hit resets it\nFile: server.sprint.sprintBoostDurationTicks
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.sprint.sprintminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted sprint hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.sprint.sprintMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.melee.meleeweakspotenabled=Melee weak spots
weakspot.server.melee.meleeweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the melee weak spots on or off\nWhile holding a sword or axe near enemies, weak spots show left and right of the crosshair. Each hit charges up the next attack\nFile: server.melee.meleeWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.melee.meleeminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.melee.meleeminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted melee hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.melee.meleeMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.melee.meleechargeperhit=Charge per hit
weakspot.server.melee.meleechargeperhit.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nCharge added per melee hit (added to the next attack multiplier), scaled by the combo factor\nA charged attack is a critical hit (x1.5) and then x(1 + charge)\nFile: server.melee.meleeChargePerHit
weakspot.server.melee.meleechargemax=Max charge
weakspot.server.melee.meleechargemax.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMaximum melee charge. 0 means no limit (default)\nSet 2.0 or so if it gets too strong\nFile: server.melee.meleeChargeMax
weakspot.server.portal.portalweakspotenabled=Portal weak spots
weakspot.server.portal.portalweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the nether portal weak spots on or off\nWhile standing in a portal, a weak spot shows near the crosshair. Hits shorten the wait before you travel\nFile: server.portal.portalWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.portal.portalhitticks=Ticks cut per hit
weakspot.server.portal.portalhitticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nPortal wait removed per hit (ticks), scaled by the combo factor. The vanilla wait is 80 ticks\nFile: server.portal.portalHitTicks
weakspot.server.portal.portalminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.portal.portalminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted portal hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.portal.portalMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.swim.swimweakspotenabled=Swim weak spots
weakspot.server.swim.swimweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the swim weak spots on or off\nWhile swimming, a weak spot shows near the crosshair; hitting it gives a short dash and faster swimming for a while\nFile: server.swim.swimWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.swim.swimboostmultiplier=Speed multiplier
weakspot.server.swim.swimboostmultiplier.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nSwim speed multiplier after hitting the swim weak spot, with the combo factor on top. Keep it the same as the vehicle multiplier so boats stay faster\nFile: server.swim.swimBoostMultiplier
weakspot.server.swim.swimboostmaxmultiplier=Max multiplier
weakspot.server.swim.swimboostmaxmultiplier.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nCap on the swim speed multiplier. 0 means no cap\nFile: server.swim.swimBoostMaxMultiplier
weakspot.server.swim.swimboostdurationticks=Boost duration (ticks)
weakspot.server.swim.swimboostdurationticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHow long the swim boost lasts (ticks). Each hit resets it to this length\nFile: server.swim.swimBoostDurationTicks
weakspot.server.swim.swimdashdistance=Dash distance
weakspot.server.swim.swimdashdistance.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nHow far the dash on a swim hit carries you (blocks, roughly). Combos do not make it longer\nFile: server.swim.swimDashDistance
weakspot.server.swim.swimminhitintervalticks=Min hit interval (ticks)
weakspot.server.swim.swimminhitintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between accepted swim hits (ticks). The client limits hits the same way\nFile: server.swim.swimMinHitIntervalTicks
weakspot.server.melee.critsperrepair=Hits per repair
weakspot.server.melee.critsperrepair.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nEvery this many landed charged melee attacks repair the held item. 0 disables it\nThe remainder carries over until logout. Server only (not sent to clients)\nFile: server.melee.critsPerRepair
weakspot.server.melee.critrepairperstep=Repair per step
weakspot.server.melee.critrepairperstep.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nDurability repaired per critsPerRepair. Server only (not sent to clients)\nFile: server.melee.critRepairPerStep
weakspot.server.general.giveguidebook=Give the guide book
weakspot.server.general.giveguidebook.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nGive players a guide book on their first login (once per player)\nIt can also be read with the Guide button on the stats screen (K key). Server only (not sent to clients)\nFile: server.general.giveGuideBook
weakspot.server.general.markersharerange=Marker share range
weakspot.server.general.markersharerange.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nRange for relaying other players' weak spot markers (blocks). Only players within this distance of a marker see it\n0 stops relaying (other players' markers are not shown)\nFile: server.general.markerShareRange
weakspot.server.general.markersendminintervalticks=Marker send interval
weakspot.server.general.markersendminintervalticks.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nMinimum interval between marker updates sent per player (ticks). Keeps network traffic down\nFile: server.general.markerSendMinIntervalTicks
weakspot.client.sound.myhitsound=My hit sound
weakspot.client.sound.myhitsound.tooltip=Note block instrument for your hit sound\nXYLOPHONE, CHIME, BELL, FLUTE, GUITAR, HARP, BASS, HAT, SNARE, BASEDRUM, PLING\nAlso on the Sound tab of the stats screen (K key), with a preview\nFile: client.sound.myHitSound
weakspot.client.sound.myhitvolume=My hit volume
weakspot.client.sound.myhitvolume.tooltip=Volume of your hit sound (0 is silent)\nThe vanilla Players volume also applies\nFile: client.sound.myHitVolume
weakspot.client.sound.hitchordenabled=Chords with combos
weakspot.client.sound.hitchordenabled.tooltip=Stack notes on your hit sound as your combo grows (2 notes from 25, 3 from 100). Off keeps a single note\nFile: client.sound.hitChordEnabled
weakspot.client.sound.othershitvolume=Others' hit volume
weakspot.client.sound.othershitvolume.tooltip=Volume of other players' hit sounds (0 is silent)\nThe vanilla Players volume also applies\nFile: client.sound.othersHitVolume
weakspot.client.sound.othershitsound=Others' hit sound
weakspot.client.sound.othershitsound.tooltip=Note block instrument for other players' hit sounds\nXYLOPHONE, CHIME, BELL, FLUTE, GUITAR, HARP, BASS, HAT, SNARE, BASEDRUM, PLING\nFile: client.sound.othersHitSound
weakspot.client.markers.othermarkerenabled=Show others' markers
weakspot.client.markers.othermarkerenabled.tooltip=Show other players' weak spot markers\nFile: client.markers.otherMarkerEnabled
weakspot.client.markers.othermarkercolor=Others' marker color
weakspot.client.markers.othermarkercolor.tooltip=Color of other players' weak spot markers (#RRGGBB). Pick one you can tell from your own\nInvalid values use the default light blue #3FA9FF\nFile: client.markers.otherMarkerColor
weakspot.client.markers.othermarkeralpha=Others' marker opacity
weakspot.client.markers.othermarkeralpha.tooltip=Opacity of other players' markers (multiplied with your own marker's; 1 is the same, 0 is invisible)\nFile: client.markers.otherMarkerAlpha
weakspot.general.configversion=Config version
weakspot.general.configversion.tooltip=[Internal] Config file migration version. Do not edit\nFile: general.configVersion
weakspot.server.mining.miningweakspotenabled=Mining weak spots
weakspot.server.mining.miningweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the mining weak spots on or off\nOff: nobody gets mining weak spots (vanilla mining)\nFile: server.mining.miningWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.mining.miningcombobonus=Combo bonus
weakspot.server.mining.miningcombobonus.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the mining combo bonus on or off\nOn: each hit digs more as the combo grows (x1.25 at 25 ... x4 at 1000)\nFile: server.mining.miningComboBonus
weakspot.server.growth.growthweakspotenabled=Growth weak spots
weakspot.server.growth.growthweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the crop and sapling growth weak spots on or off\nOff: nobody gets them, and empty-hand right clicks work as usual\nFile: server.growth.growthWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.machine.machineweakspotenabled=Machine weak spots
weakspot.server.machine.machineweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the machine weak spots on or off\nOff: nobody gets them, and sneaking with an empty hand opens the GUI as usual\nFile: server.machine.machineWeakSpotEnabled
weakspot.server.animal.animalweakspotenabled=Animal weak spots
weakspot.server.animal.animalweakspotenabled.tooltip=In multiplayer, the server's setting takes priority.\nTurn the animal weak spots on or off\nOff: nobody gets them, and empty-hand right clicks work as usual\nFile: server.animal.animalWeakSpotEnabled
